WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.069
The final set of secrets for the final DLC of The last Souls game.

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.959
And it's fitting that in this DLC, there are some of the best secrets of all.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.280
Case in point, number one:

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:20.860
...What if it was never here in the first place?"

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.480
The Purging monument, you can see it

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.160
But how do you get there?

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.820
This question completely absorbed like over ten hours of my play time,

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.160
and the only location I could conceivably find that could possibly lead there

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.040
is this chute leading upwards.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.000
and behind a broken statue, engraved upon the wall, are the words,

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:46.649
"Show your humanity".

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:51.270
I was lucky enough to play the DLC a couple of days before it was public

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:56.489
And I couldn't rely on Vaati's amazing videos to help me figure this riddle out.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.140
So I tested all kinds of things for hours and hours on end:

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.089
I tried to get the Herald headpiece,

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:06.100
I cast all kinds of Abyss Magic,

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.820
I tried Chameleon,

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.440
I did all the friendly human gestures,

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.100
I died in front of it,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.020
I did everything on my massive checklist.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.960
Until I discovered:

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.580
I was using Chameleon... in the wrong place.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.380
See, Chameleon is based off your immediate environment, not the general vicinity,

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:33.040
which is what I thought it was, so, if you cast it atop the abyssal swamp, then you will turn into a

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.290
humanity sprite.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.290
Which reveals a ladder.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:46.160
Which leads to a final judicator giant, two ringed knights, and the Purging Monument of the Ringed City.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:17.149
"...No matter what might come out, no matter what i was, if you would do me the honor.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.500
allow me to be a true friend... always."

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.260
Of course, Lapp deserves his own video,

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:30.640
but find the purging monument before he goes hollow and you'll restore your dear friend's memories,

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.760
and In the Shared Grave, he shows his true self.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:54.140
Patches is one of the very few undead who made it to the end of the world.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.980
Think about that, he made it through all those cycles

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:00.600
and ages of fire  to get here like you, and like Gael did.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.280
So bearing that in mind, I think that his words carry a lot of weight.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.280
His ashes say: "He never lost heart and never looked back.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:13.540
He marched in one direction and that direction was dead ahead."

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.400
Number three: Beyond the shared grave is Dark Eater Midir,

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:25.320
the archdragon who was tasked to eternally battle and consume the dark.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.980
As you progress through the Ringed City, look behind you sometimes.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.000
Midir takes perch upon multiple towers of the Ringed City,

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.656
watching and waiting for the perfect moment to strike.

00:04:38.656 --> 00:04:42.563
Oh, that's nice of him: he chose a bridge where I can take cover -

00:04:42.563 --> 00:04:47.239
dash out, attack, and just rinse and repeat -  until Midir falls into the chasm.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:12.890
"Just before the church of the princess standeth the tower

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.800
honoring ancient knights.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.080
There lies the small shrine

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.470
Behind the sculpted knight which beareth no arms.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:26.899
'Tis from there, one may descend the chasm of Darkness. I prithee,

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.930
put the great dragon to rest."

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:35.814
Midir, descendant of archdragons, was raised by the gods,

00:05:35.814 --> 00:05:37.730
and due to his immortality,

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.600
he was the perfect candidate to battle the dark,

00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:46.519
for he would never forget his eternal duty, even after the gods perished.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:53.710
From Midir, you discover a covenant with the Spears of the Church,

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.789
knights who are sworn to the defense of Princess Filianore.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.400
There's a small shrine to the Spears that you can find outside the Church of Filianore.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:09.460
Here you can contribute Spear Ornaments, one of which drops from the Argo bossfight.

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:13.210
Offer one and Shira will acknowledge your covenant.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:31.840
And with the covenant equipped, you will be summoned by the judicator

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:35.440
into the worlds of those who trespass upon the church of Filianore.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:42.249
Kill a trespasser, and you'll receive a Spear Ornament, proof of your fulfillment of duty.

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:46.479
If you are offer ten, then you receive a Young Grass Dew.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.230
Offer 30, and you receive a Divine Spear Fragment

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.680
which is used against online foes.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.909
And it's at this point that you'll be named a divine spear the church by Shira.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:21.500
This game isn't live for me right now, so I can't test this,

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.270
but assumedly players are summoned into the boss fight itself

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:31.360
instead of Halflight to fight against other players, you know, Old Monk style and Mirror Knight style,

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.824
Which is such a shame because I've already killed Argo,

00:07:34.824 --> 00:07:39.129
and that means I can't test this for myself unless I make a new character.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.100
If only there was a way to revive him.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.293
Oh, you can.

00:07:44.293 --> 00:07:47.587
Just travel back to the Purging Monument (for some reason)

00:07:47.587 --> 00:07:51.480
and for the low low price of a hundred and three thousand souls,

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:55.000
you too can experience the fight, all over again.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:00.300
Next, number six: The Lightning Arrow miracle that Shira uses.

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:05.620
In this room, before you fight Argo and after you first face Midir,

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.319
is an illusory wall,

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.000
and behind it, there's another illusory wall,

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.499
and behind that is another illusionary wall.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:15.200
And then there's the Lightning Arrow:

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:20.670
A miracle that was used by the few female knights who served in the war against the dragons.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:24.089
Number seven: I want to talk about Filianore,

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:30.520
specifically her name, because one thing we really really haven't touched on at all in my videos is the

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.900
etymology of certain names in Souls.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:38.100
Miyazaki clearly pulls from all kinds of languages when he designs these names,

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.920
and a lot of them are really quite beautiful, and Filianore is the perfect example.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:47.720
She is the youngest daughter of Gwyn, lord of sunlight.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:52.700
And there are two components to this name Filianore that were posted first

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.679
I think on Reddit by a user named knightfrost.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:09:00.160
So the first part of her name 'Filia' means 'daughter' in Latin,

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.300
and the second part, 'Anor', mean  'sun'  in Elvish,

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:08.500
and is of course what inspired the name Anor Londo.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:13.770
Filia-nore, the daughter of the sun, the daughter of Gwyn.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.040
There is another interpretation you can go with.

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:23.189
This was posted by (DarkSoulInUs?), and he or she says that the word 'Nore' is Latin for

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:30.000
'daughter-in-law' which casts some new meaning on whether Filianore could actually have had a

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.790
different mother to the other children of Gwyn.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:40.400
And, with Yoshka somehow being revealed to be a child of Gwyn as well, it becomes less and less

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:45.580
surprising that we're learning about more and more of Gwyn's many children.

00:09:45.599 --> 00:09:48.720
Number eight: The ring burdened Pygmy statues.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.150
A revelation in this DLC,

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:55.169
is the circumstances surrounding the first men and the gods.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.300
So as an example,

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:02.819
from the Ringed Knight set, we learned that early men were originally very close to the abyss

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:09.900
and that while their warriors actually fought with the gods against the arch dragons in that famous war,

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.630
they also suffered at the gods' hands afterwards,

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:15.660
for the gods seemed to fear the abyss.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:21.150
So they branded the armor and the weaponry of the knights with a seal of fire

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:23.838
Occluding the darkness of the abyss,

00:10:23.838 --> 00:10:27.270
and this brand, of course, has appeared time and time again,

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.789
this great burden to Mankind,

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.374
and here in the Ringed City, we learn more about how it came about

00:10:34.374 --> 00:10:39.164
and we'll go into this so much more in other videos, so subscribe if you haven't already.

00:10:39.164 --> 00:10:42.210
I just want to say I love that the burden of the seal is

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:44.729
represented so literally by these statues.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:50.400
Next, we've mentioned this before, but depending on whether you kill the Demon from Below

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.809
or the Demon in Pain first,

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:57.599
that determines whether you get the fireball Demon Prince or the laser Demon Prince,

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:03.845
and originally the Demon Prince fight actually featured only one bat at the start,

00:11:03.845 --> 00:11:06.179
with the second one appearing halfway.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:10.975
Additionally, I also want to point out that the description of the Soul of the Demon Prince

00:11:10.975 --> 00:11:12.750
has changed from what I said earlier.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.950
It now reads the demons, birthed from a common chaos,

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.410
share almost everything between them,

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:26.639
even the pride of their Prince and his near faded flame, so that the last demon standing may rekindled it.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:34.020
The description before this revealed that this was indeed the Demon Prince that was defeated by Lothric,

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:36.450
and that in this hollow tree,

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:42.089
he lost the memory of flame that burned within him, which marked the end of demonkind.

00:11:42.089 --> 00:11:44.249
And they removed this description

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.850
so I think they were trying to

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:52.380
imply the death of demonkind more in this new description, because now,

00:11:52.779 --> 00:11:59.818
neither the Demon in Flame (Pain) nor the Demon from Below remain alive to rekindle the final flame of chaos.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:02.100
And finally, number ten.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.699
Kill the Stone-Humped Hag at the beginning and

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.470
this happens:

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:11.670
"My time has come, has it?

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.649
Well,

00:12:14.649 --> 00:12:18.660
maybe I'll get to see an angel...

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.640
Sure enough, an angel does appear.

00:12:20.769 --> 00:12:24.972
But this one is curious compared to the others. As far as I can tell,

00:12:24.972 --> 00:12:30.870
it doesn't actually reappear once you kill it, like the other ones, for it has no

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:34.894
discernible fleshy-avatar-parasite-thing on the ground,

00:12:34.894 --> 00:12:38.880
like the others that grow over the corpses of Pilgrims.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.779
Perhaps this angel is a resurrection of the hag,

00:12:42.779 --> 00:12:46.940
but the parasite has yet to grow inside of her.

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:48.508
Unless there's something I'm missing here,

00:12:48.519 --> 00:12:56.600
there is no material benefit to killing the hag, nor from killing any NPC in the Ringed City, really.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:13:00.839
Lapp, the Corvian, the pygmy, the locusts, none drop a thing.

00:13:01.449 --> 00:13:05.729
So I'm currently lacking about four more things to make another one of these videos,

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:09.750
and I know there's more out there that I haven't found yet.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:16.520
So if there's anything that you've discovered, post it here in the comments, and I'll try give you a shoutout in the next one.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.600
So good luck out there. Enjoy the Ringed City,

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:23.460
and I'll enjoy making videos for you to enjoy when you're done. See you soon.

